When the page is zoomed, Ladybird fits an image document’s image
against the viewport at 100% zoom, so zooming in enlarges it past the
window. Blink does the same: ImageDocument::Scale() pretends the
viewport is larger when the page is zoomed in, and ResizeImageToFit()
sets the fitted size from it. Gecko’s ImageDocument::ShrinkToFit()
keeps an already fitted image’s size while the zoom level differs from
mOriginalZoomLevel, which also lets zoom enlarge it. And WebKit’s
ImageDocument::scale() always fits against the window’s current
visible size, whatever the zoom.
